===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|military}} Relating to, using, or typical of guerrilla warfare, or its principles of small independent or non-official perpetrators.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1908|author=George Devereux Oswell|title=Sketches of Rulers of India|volume=I|chapter=VII|page=127
|passage=Wherever Nicholson was most wanted, there he was sure to be found. What his life was at this time may be seen from a letter he wrote to his mother: 'I am leading a very '''guerrilla''' sort of life with seven hundred horse and foot raised among the people of the country. The chieftain who is in rebellion has eight regular regiments and sixteen guns, so that I am unable to meet them openly in the field.'}}
#* '''1963''', {{w|Samuel B. Griffith}} (translator), {{w|Mao Zedong}}, ''{{w|On Protracted War|The Red Book of Guerrilla Warfare}}'', edited by Shawn Conners, {{ISBN|1-934255-27-0}}, published 2010, page 14, original 1937
#*: On the other hand, after the fall of Feng Ling Tu, the operations of Central Shansi, and Suiyuan, troops were more '''guerrilla''' than orthodox in nature.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1976|author={{w|Walter Laqueur}}|title={{w|Guerrilla Warfare}}|page=205
|passage=The Slovak uprising in the latter days was not '''guerrilla''' in character, which, incidentally, may have been one of the reasons for its failure.}}
# {{lb|en|marketing}} Relating to, using, or typical of [[guerrilla marketing]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1989|author=Michael Wiese|title=Film & video marketing|page=445
|passage=We took a very '''guerrilla''' approach to marketing ''Goin' Hollywood'', in keeping with the irreverent tone of the game.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Firefox Continues To Chip Away At IE's Share| work=InformationWeek| date=February 28, 2005| passage="Mozilla's marketing has been very '''guerrilla'''. You're not seeing it spend millions of dollars on TV. Instead, it's a powerful ground swell.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|work=The Times|date=February 26, 2010| title=A serious woman| passage=My style is more '''guerrilla'''. I grew up in a village, a very suppressed environment. I was like one of those young kids who hated the whole conventional way of doing things. So when I started to make films it was very hand-made, very fast.}}
# Using [[unconventional]], [[non-traditional]], non-[[mainstream]] and often [[subversive]] practices to achieve something.
#: {{ux|en|[[guerrilla marketing|'''guerrilla''' marketing]]}}
#: {{ux|en|'''guerrilla''' tourism}}
#: {{ux|en|'''guerrilla''' gardening}}

